WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.007
This is PasteGuard for the MLH Solana Hackathon.

00:00:03.344 --> 00:00:06.409
A Pastebin post promised a twenty-five percent swap bonus.

00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:08.963
The script quietly changed the deposit wallet.

00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:11.491
PasteGuard reads the script on your device.

00:00:11.828 --> 00:00:17.586
It points to the remote dependency, the browser network hook, and the exact line that swaps the address.

00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:19.360
Here is where the money would go.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.960
Solana devnet simulates both transfers.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.911
Same amount, two different wallets.

00:00:24.305 --> 00:00:27.742
We can see the balance changes without a signature or a broadcast.

00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:37.294
The case library covers four real campaigns: the original Pastebin lure, a fake Solana sniper, a phony AI compiler, and a seed phrase trap.

00:00:37.744 --> 00:00:40.902
Paste code into the web app, or scan a selection from Chrome.

00:00:41.355 --> 00:00:43.700
We built this in one day as a hackathon prototype.

00:00:44.037 --> 00:00:47.729
The campaign screenshots are real, and the devnet preview is live.

